---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Complete User Guide" currentPath="/docs/guides/user-guide">
  <div class="space-y-8 font-mono text-xs">
    <div>
      <div class="text-[11px] text-zinc-400 font-semibold mb-1">USER MANUAL</div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-sans">Complete RouteNex User Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm font-sans mt-1">Mastering provider configuration, virtual keys, and traffic monitoring.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#111113] border border-[#222226] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">Virtual Access Keys (Local BYOK)</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        RouteNex isolates client traffic through Virtual Keys (<code class="text-zinc-200">rn_live_...</code>). These keys are stored on disk as SHA-256 hashes, with configurable RPM rate limits, daily USD spend caps, and model allowlists.
      </p>
      <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-[#18181b] border border-[#27272a] text-zinc-300">
        <div>1. Open <a href="/dashboard" class="text-white underline">API Keys Manager</a></div>
        <div>2. Click "+ Create Virtual Key"</div>
        <div>3. Assign an RPM limit and allowed model slugs</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#111113] border border-[#222226] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">Provider Pooling (Multiply Rate Limits)</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        By connecting multiple free keys for Groq, Cerebras, or Mistral, RouteNex automatically pools them via round-robin or headroom distribution, multiplying your effective throughput limit without billing upgrades.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
